  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#34950\", \"PowerToys#46333\", \"PowerToys#48566\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been made before: hiding selected windows from screen sharing, recording and screenshots (via WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE). It is tracked in PowerToys#46333 (Privacy Overlay), which is the main issue; PowerToys#48566 was closed as a duplicate of it. PowerToys#34950 asks for the same thing (window masking by name or hotkey), and its earlier /dup to #13035 was disputed because that issue is about something different. It is not implemented yet. A proof-of-concept exists in #46333, using an injected hook DLL, because setting the display affinity directly from another process is blocked. Please subscribe to #46333 and add a thumbs-up there rather than opening a new ticket. In the meantime, third-party tools such as Invisiwind or WinHider can hide windows from capture, though they may miss newly opened windows.\"}",
